{
  "_doc": "The logo stage: the full-window logo shows behind the header mark's hold, the typed words and stencil.EasterEggs. The desktop reads this file over its qrc alias (resources/app.qrc) and both surfaces resolve a show from this one table: a show's `accents` are the presets that open it on a hold, `motion` the motion mode that hold also needs, `customHex` the custom accent that opens it ('*' = any other custom hex). Every show is also its own facade call and, lower-cased, its typed word. The webcore row (the session skin in webcore.json) shares grey with dustySpot and is told apart by `motion` alone, as every styled row is: dust flying opens the dust show, a still interface opens the skin. `typeGapMs` is how long a half-typed word waits for its next letter before it is forgotten. Sizes are shares of the shorter window side; times are ms.",
